message: "If you use SkyShift, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SkyShift: zoom through time in NASA SPHEREx sky images"
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23181747
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mahadi5577/skyshift"
url: "https://mahadi5577.github.io/skyshift/"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23181747
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23181748
    description: "Version 0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  SkyShift is an open-source web tool and analysis toolkit for exploring how the sky changes in
  NASA SPHEREx near-infrared survey images. It selects wavelength-matched SPHEREx exposures of any
  sky position at four time scales (hours, days, months and a year), reads only the needed pixels
  from the public archive, and presents them as blink, slider and difference views with known
  Solar System objects labelled. A citizen-science mode trains users on planted synthetic movers
  calibrated by injection-recovery tests before they flag candidates in untouched data.
